      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing leaves on a Monstera deliciosa are most commonly caused by overwatering or root rot, as these plants have incredibly sensitive roots that rot easily when soil stays soggy. While nutrient deficiencies can cause thin, pale yellow leaves, they rarely turn an entire leaf entirely yellow before dropping off. Since you suspect watering issues, check the top few inches of soil; if it's still wet, let it dry out completely before your next watering to allow roots to breathe.",
